Original commit body from 81a032c1f2624d110d66a7443198a4e8db5d02e1:

verify_claims.untyped_receiver_sites -- the channel that makes a clean
boundary or taint verdict NAME the sink call sites whose receiver it could
not type -- selects on meta.call_construct == "method". java, objc and rust
emit the external call edge and never stamped that key, so each reached a
BARE `confirmed` and disclosed nothing.

Measured across the nine catalogued languages that declare method-kind
sinks, one fixture apiece calling a sink from that language's OWN catalogue
on an untypable receiver:

  inert but stampable  java 139, objc 122, rust 34   = 295 sinks
  no edge to stamp     kotlin 181, javascript 51     = 232 sinks (WI-nasuf)
  already firing       scala 162, python 143,
                       swift 97, go 25               = 427 sinks

java's stamp moved OUT of the branch that made the key mean something
narrower than its name: it was set only where the receiver's type resolved
AND was imported, so `call_construct` silently meant "a method call whose
receiver I typed". It is now set once, for every receiver-bearing call. The
phantom-barrier reasoning already recorded there is unchanged and still
load-bearing. objc stamps unconditionally -- a message send IS a method call
by construction. rust stamps on its existing is_method_call.

RECALL COST NONE, and gate_named_entry is where that is visible: with no
module hint it refuses a method-kind hit EITHER WAY, through the
call_construct arm with the stamp and through the non_method filter without
it. The stamp only buys the ability to say so.

Measured at three layers. Published output: a java file whose only fs_write
reach is `u.mkdirs()` on an untypable receiver moved from bare `confirmed`
(rc 0) to `confirmed_with_caveats` (rc 3) naming the sites, while the
CONTROL ARM -- same claim, a typed java.io.File receiver -- stays `violated`
(rc 1). objc moved likewise.

The parity gate is the durable part, not the three stamps.
test_disclosure_parity.py is driven from the shipped io_primitives
catalogues rather than a hand-written list, so a language arriving LATER
with method-kind sinks and no fixture fails there instead of reaching a
silent clean verdict while every existing test stays green. The two no-edge
languages are a bounded exemption pinned by its own test.

A first draft of the measurement was wrong and the correction is recorded
rather than quietly fixed: written with a CAST receiver, scala and swift
both read as inert and the headline came out at 82% rather than 55%. A cast
takes a different bare-call branch in both; the plain receiver.method()
shape was already stamped correctly.

